Experiment No. 07 


Aim:
To develop a Java application using
built-in and user-defined packages.



Procedure:
Create a user-defined package named employee.
Create an Employee class with ID, name and salary.
Import the package and get employee details using Scanner.
Create an object and display the employee details.


Result:
Thus, the Java program using built-in and user-defined
packages was successfully executed.

##PROGRAM

##Employee.java

package employee;

public class Employee {
    int id;
    String name;

    public Employee(int i, String n) {
        id = i;
        name = n;
    }

    public void display() {
        System.out.println("ID: " + id);
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
    }
}


## Main.java


import employee.Employee;
import java.util.*;

class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter ID: ");
        int id = sc.nextInt();

        sc.nextLine();
        System.out.print("Enter Name: ");
        String name = sc.nextLine();

        Employee e = new Employee(id, name);
        e.display();

        sc.close();
    }
}
